@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100

# ---------------- Day 4: tokens ----------------
# Create your own development tokens once (in the project folder):
#   dotnet user-jwts create --name alice --role Admin
#   dotnet user-jwts create --name bob
# and paste each token below. A token is valid for three months.
@aliceToken = paste-alice-token-here
@bobToken = paste-bob-token-here

### Public list, still anonymous: Aurora, Sentinel
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes

### Anonymous write: 401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer (not a login page)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Nobody",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Alice creates a Draft: 201, "owner": "alice"
# @name aliceHero
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Nightwatch",
  "originStory": "A night guard who protects the old harbor district.",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Bob creates a Draft: 201, "owner": "bob"
# @name bobHero
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Skylark",
  "originStory": "A courier who learned to fly above the rooftops of the old town.",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Alice adds Shield to her Draft: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{aliceHero.response.body.$.id}}/powers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### A wrong token: 401, WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Authorization: Bearer not-a-token

### Minimal API, same rule: anonymous 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Nobody",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Minimal API with a token: 201, "owner": "bob"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Minimal Bob",
  "originStory": "Created through the Minimal API with a bearer token.",
  "race": "Mutant",
  "alignment": "Neutral"
}

# ---------------- Lab 2: who may do what ----------------

### Bob (no Admin role) retires Sentinel: 403 (Demo 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/1/retire
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Alice (Admin) retires Sentinel: 200, Retired (Demo 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/1/retire
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### Bob tries to delete Alice's Draft: 403 (Lab 2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{aliceHero.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Alice deletes a Registered hero (Aurora): 409, the domain rule comes after authorization (Lab 2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/2
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### Alice deletes her own Draft: 204 (Lab 2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{aliceHero.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
